# UC-007 · Outbound HTTP

> Partial of `docs/use-cases/UC-007-capture-payment/`. Owner: `http-client-architect`.
> Inherits the outbound port and its domain types from `10-domain.md`, and the external call and
> its authentication answer from `00-use-case.md` § External calls — doesn't redecide them.
> Contains no code. Form references in `.claude/skills/http-client-architect/templates/`.
> Rules applied, never reproduced: `@.claude/rules/http-client.md`,
> `@.claude/rules/error-handling.md` § Integration families, `@.claude/rules/api-rest.md` § Errors — 500 family.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Mother spec | `00-use-case.md` — External calls: the payment service provider charges the card; OAuth2 client credentials; supports `Idempotency-Key` |
| Why this partial exists | `10-domain.md` § Ports declares `PaymentGatewayPort`, kind `external HTTP` |
| Adapter package | `adapter.out.http.paymentgateway` (blueprint `packages.map`, entry `adapter.out.http`) |
| Divergences from other partials | none |

## 1 · Operations

One row per remote operation the port needs. The provider's documentation is the source; its link
goes in the row.

| Port method | Dependency (group) | Remote call | Idempotent? | Key source | Read timeout | Domain outcomes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `charge(PaymentId, Money, IdempotencyKey)` | `payment-gateway` | `POST /v1/charges` ([docs](https://psp.example/docs/charges#create)) | yes — `Idempotency-Key`, honored 24 h by the provider | `Payment.chargeKey`, created with the payment (§ 10) | 3 s (p99.9 measured 1.8 s) | 422 `insufficient-funds` / `card-declined` → `BusinessRuleViolationException` `PAYMENT_DECLINED` |
| `findStatus(ChargeReference)` | `payment-gateway` | `GET /v1/charges/{id}` | yes — safe | — | 3 s | 404 → `Optional.empty()` |

Every other failure is an integration family through the shared translator
(`@.claude/rules/error-handling.md` § Integration families): 429/503/connect → unavailable,
502/504/read timeout/reset → outcome unknown, the rest → bad response.

## 2 · Client

| Dependency | Client | Matrix row | Exemplar |
|---|---|---|---|
| `payment-gateway` | HTTP interface (`@HttpExchange`) | `references/client-decision-matrix.md` § 1 row 3: stable contract, servlet stack, no OpenAPI document published | `HttpExchangeAdapter.java.example` |

Rejected, one line each: **OpenAPI Generator** — the provider publishes no OpenAPI document.
**`RestClient` direct** — no dynamic URL, no streaming, no `Link` pagination. **`WebClient`** —
nothing streamed. **OpenFeign** — legacy only; nothing in the project uses it.

## 3 · Engine and pool

| Decision | Value | State |
|---|---|---|
| Engine | Apache HttpClient 5, pinned by `spring.http.clients.imperative.factory: http-components` | NEW — first outbound call of the project |
| Pool | 20 per route, 100 total — 40 req/s × 0.25 s p99 ≈ 10 concurrent, doubled | NEW |
| Lease timeout | 500 ms | NEW |
| Idle eviction / time-to-live | 30 s / 5 min — the provider's load balancer closes idle connections at 60 s (asked) | NEW |
| Engine retry | off | NEW |
| Exemplar | `ApacheHttpClient5Config.java.example` | — |

## 4 · Outbound authentication

| Dependency | Scheme | Where the credential lives | Exemplar |
|---|---|---|---|
| `payment-gateway` | OAuth2 client credentials, scopes `charges:write charges:read` | `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_CLIENT_ID`, `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_CLIENT_SECRET` (environment), token URI `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_TOKEN_URI` | `OAuth2ClientCredentialsConfig.java.example` |

Token cached and renewed by the authorized-client manager — never fetched per call. TLS on, no
redirect followed.

## 5 · Retry and resilience

| Dependency | Retrying layer | Attempts · backoff | Retried on | Breaker | Bulkhead | Fallback |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `payment-gateway` | the adapter (`@Retryable` + `DependencyRetryPredicate`) — the trigger is an HTTP request, nothing upstream retries | 3 · 200 ms ×2, max 2 s, jitter 100 ms | unavailable without `Retry-After`; outcome unknown (both methods `@IdempotentCall`) | `outbound` config: 50 % of 20 calls, open 30 s | 20, no wait — equals the pool's per-route limit | none — a failed charge is not a success; the 503 reaches the caller |

