## 8 · Declared dependencies

| Dependency | Version | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-restclient` | (managed by the Boot parent) | `RestClient` and HTTP interfaces — Boot 4 no longer brings it with the web starter (Initializr `spring-restclient`) |
| `org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5` | (managed by the Boot parent) | engine, § 3 |
| `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-security-oauth2-client` | (managed by the Boot parent) | client credentials, § 4 (Initializr `oauth2-client`) |
| `io.github.resilience4j:resilience4j-spring-boot4` | the `<release>` of its `maven-metadata.xml`, read at design time and written here — not managed by the Boot parent | breaker and bulkhead, § 5 |
| `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-aspectj` | (managed by the Boot parent) | Resilience4j's annotations and aspects |

The test support (`org.wiremock.integrations:wiremock-spring-boot`) is declared by `40-tests.md` § 5.

## 9 · Contract test cases

Through the port, against WireMock — `test-architect`'s `HttpClientAdapterIT.java.example`.

| Port method | Case | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| `charge` | 201 | reference mapped; request carried `Idempotency-Key` = the payment's key, and the mapped body |
| `findStatus` | 200 with an unknown field and status | `ChargeStatus.UNKNOWN` |
| `findStatus` | 404 | `Optional.empty()` |
| `charge` | 422 Problem Details `insufficient-funds` | `BusinessRuleViolationException` `PAYMENT_DECLINED`, one attempt |
| `charge` | 503 | `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_UNAVAILABLE`, exactly 3 attempts |
| `charge` | 503 + `Retry-After: 30` | one attempt, `retryAfter` = 30 s |
| `charge` | 400 | `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_BAD_RESPONSE`, one attempt |
| `findStatus` | delay > read timeout | `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN`, 3 attempts |
| `findStatus` | connection reset | `OutcomeUnknownException` |

## 10 · Requirements to other partials

| To | Requirement | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `20-persistence.md` | `Payment.chargeKey` (UUID, not null, unique) persisted with the payment, before the call | the key must survive a restart; generating it at call time makes every retry a new charge |
| `35-jobs.md` | a reconciliation pass over payments left `CAPTURE_UNKNOWN`, calling `findStatus` | `OutcomeUnknownException` on `charge` after the retries: the charge may exist |
| `10-domain.md` | `CAPTURE_UNKNOWN` state on `Payment`, entered on `OutcomeUnknownException` | already modeled — cited, not redesigned |
| `32-security.md` | none — the project already has a `SecurityFilterChain`; adding the OAuth2 client starter changes no endpoint | checked: chain on disk |

## 11 · Deferred

none

## Design patterns

| Force or symptom | Pattern | Classes and interfaces it creates | "When not" checked |
|---|---|---|---|
| Every provider needs the same failure translation, and none may decide it alone | none — a shared helper, not a pattern; the translator is a plain class composed by each adapter | — | Decorator considered for `ResilientHttpCall` and rejected: one wrapper, no stack to compose |

## Impact on approved use cases

none — first outbound HTTP call of the project.

## Implementation order

1. The dependencies of § 8
2. The integration families in `domain.exception`
3. `adapter.out.http.shared`: translator, predicate, `IdempotentCall`, `OutboundHttpConfig`, engine, OAuth2 config
4. `adapter.out.http.paymentgateway`: DTOs, HTTP interface, client config, mapper, adapter
5. `ApiExceptionHandler` — the three 5xx handlers
6. Properties in `application.yml`
7. Tests — `40-tests.md`
